A cell written in place in one arm of an `if` or a `case`, or in both, and read after it; a list written in one arm and read through a call that answers it (#2594). The arms are never one run, so what the join holds from the arm that did not write is no holder of the write: each write is accepted and runs in place (ownership-v3-kernel.md §6 rule 7, amended). Its live twin is CellWrittenInArmLive.
